# SYNTAX TEST "text.html.tiddlywiki5" "An inline run opens only where it closes on the same line"

Prose naming __localVar in passing, and the rest reads plain.
#              ^^^^^^^^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5

A stray '' apostrophe pair leaves the line alone.
#          ^^^^^^^^^^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5

A lone ` backtick leaves the line alone.
#        ^^^^^^^^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5

Here //an italic run// closes where it opened.
#      ^^^^^^^^^^^^^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5 markup.italic.tiddlywiki5

Here ''a bold run'' closes where it opened.
#      ^^^^^^^^^^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5 markup.bold.tiddlywiki5

See http://example.com/a and //genuine italic// together.
#   ^^^^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5 markup.underline.link.external.tiddlywiki5 markup.underline.link.external.http.tiddlywiki5
#                              ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5 markup.italic.tiddlywiki5

An ordinary sentence after the blank line.
#<- text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5
